# pstack — ReadyForRobots Cloud defaults

Cloud agents often have no `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc`. Use inherit-parent / auto unless the operator has a local setup-pstack rule. Real slugs belong only in a home rule after setup-pstack confirms them.

# pstack model configuration. One line per role. inherit-parent / auto = parent chat model.
feature, refactoring: inherit-parent
bug-fix: inherit-parent
perf-issue: inherit-parent
hillclimb: inherit-parent
judgment and prose: inherit-parent
hardest tasks: inherit-parent
how explorer: inherit-parent
how explainer: inherit-parent
how critics: inherit-parent
why investigators: inherit-parent
why synthesizer: inherit-parent
reflect tooling: inherit-parent
reflect judgment, divergent, synthesizer: inherit-parent
arena runners: inherit-parent
arena cross-judge pool: inherit-parent
swarm workers: inherit-parent
architect runners: inherit-parent
interrogate reviewers: inherit-parent

RFR role map when the home rule is missing:

- How = ownership before FIND / matcher / CRM edits (`pstackSite.ts` how)
- Act = implement Jobs path only (`pstackSite.ts` act)
- Critic = `scripts/pstack_release.py` + verify-readyforrobots: FIND `/`, real OEM URL, abort silent, leftover CRM, signup wall, matcher
- unslop = Jobs UI copy

Jobs work uses How plus pstack_release.py plus verify-readyforrobots. After UI copy, unslop.

Never Hermes. Never Vercel AI Gateway. pstack is the Jobs **release gate**, not a Fly model API, not a customer chat, not protocol chrome on FIND/CRM.

FIND is `/`. Submit path is `POST /api/robot-job-search`. Matcher is `POST /api/robot-job-match`. See `docs/pstack_jobs.md` and `docs/hermes_retired.md`.
**No Jobs product PR without pstack checks.**
